    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Willow Creek sits along the Trinity River, anchoring the community in a rugged canyon setting.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willow_Creek%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Originally named China Flat after Chinese laborers, the town’s post office opened in 1878 and was renamed Willow Creek in 1915.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willow_Creek%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Described as a rugged mountain community in Six Rivers National Forest, Willow Creek is reachable via State Routes 299 and 96, the Bigfoot Scenic Byway.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willow_Creek%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Indigenous residents of Willow Creek belong to the Tsnungwe or South Fork Hupa, speaking the Hupa language.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willow_Creek%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Willow Creek experiences a hot-summer Mediterranean climate, with extremely hot summers and light snowfall in winter.",
